WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.437
We talked about all the ways that we tackle

2
00:00:03.437 --> 00:00:07.470
the navigation, the big stuff in life.

3
00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.540
One of the ways I also have a coping mechanism is

4
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.160
with my remote control.

5
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.260
God, I've never loved entertainment more.

6
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:16.300
It is escapism.

7
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.220
It is entertainment.

8
00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.240
It is education.

9
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.280
There's things to relate to, things to learn from.

10
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.150
You've given us a lifetime of entertainment

11
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.770
and so much joy.

12
00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:29.290
Thank you for that.

13
00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:30.640
Oh, well, thank you.

14
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.630
I mean, people seem to keep wanting to put me

15
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.540
in that little box in your living room and

16
00:00:37.776 --> 00:00:41.560 line:15%
I was raised, I'm a second generation American.

17
00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:44.470 line:15%
I was raised in a crummy rental in Hollywood.

18
00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:47.400 line:15%
Like this was not on the radar

19
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.300
for my universe to be on sitcoms.

20
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.130
But people, again, seemed to like looking at me

21
00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:55.860
and having me make them laugh.

22
00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.190
I'm happy to do it.

23
00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.210
And it's a very strange reality,

24
00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.520
especially after leaving the industry for 12 years

25
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.410
and getting my undergrad degree and my graduate degree

26
00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:05.720
and having two kids,

27
00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.540
to return and people still want to see me!

28
00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.373
Just like that.

29
00:01:09.373 --> 00:01:10.470
So here I am.

30
00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.750
Again.
I definitely do.

31
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:13.920
We all definitely do.

32
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.670
And you play the owner of a cat cafe,

33
00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:20.053
but is it true that you've never been to one?

34
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.660
No, because of COVID

35
00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.110
and the timing of when this show started,

36
00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.720
I was supposed to go to a cat cafe and then quarantine hit.

37
00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.480
So we spent basically an entire year

38
00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.820
just waiting to film this show

39
00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.240
and I never got to go to an actual cat cafe.

40
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.353
Well, I want to introduce you to two

41
00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.880
little beings in my life

42
00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.200
that I actually got from a cat cafe.

43
00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.050
Do we have a picture of Lucky and Peach, control room?

44
00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:45.430
Yes, okay.
Aww!

45
00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:48.830
The one on the right who's gray, that's Lucky!

46
00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:53.500
And then the other, like multicolored one is Peach!

47
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.490
Beautiful.

48
00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:58.350
And I adopted them from a cat cafe.

49
00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.840
That's unbelievable.

50
00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.250
Dreams do come true.

51
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:02.083
Right?

52
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:04.120
We have so much in common again!

53
00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:08.150
And we wanted to give you a virtual cat cafe experience

54
00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:12.660
and Meow Parlour was New York's first cat cafe.

55
00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.760
I got mine in Los Angeles and through their nonprofit

56
00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:19.230
they have helped adopt a thousand feline friends--

57
00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.670
Wow.
Since opening in 2014.

58
00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:25.050
And if it's okay, Mayim, I would love to bring them out.

59
00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:26.950
Please welcome the founders of Meow Parlour,

60
00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:29.563
Christina Ha and Emily LaGrand.

61
00:02:30.424 --> 00:02:33.280
Hi!
(audience cheering)

62
00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.260
I'm so excited to have us together.

63
00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:39.780
Emily, what made you guys want to open the cat cafe

64
00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.840
and help kitties?

65
00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:45.870 line:15%
Yeah, so a few years ago I started working at

66
00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:49.970 line:15%
Christina's a pastry shop that specializes in macaroons

67
00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:53.510 line:15%
And around the same time, I took a trip

68
00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:56.080 line:15%
to Paris to visit my family.

69
00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:58.780 line:15%
And a cat cafe had just opened there.

70
00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.380
I loved it.

71
00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.733
And when I came back,

72
00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.100
I couldn't stop talking about it to Christina.

73
00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:11.070
And around the same time, a store across the street

74
00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:13.478
from the bakery became available.

75
00:03:13.478 --> 00:03:15.963
And it was steadily a joke at first.

76
00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.370
But I guess it became serious

77
00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:21.720
because that's how Meow Parlor was born.

78
00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.680
Well, and Mayim, do you have a question

79
00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.440
for Christina and Emily?

80
00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.301
I do.

81
00:03:28.301 --> 00:03:31.220
Pretending to be a cat cafe owner

82
00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:33.540
apparently is a lot like being a cat cafe owner

83
00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:36.330
in that I'm surrounded by cats all day.

84
00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:40.480
And when I come home, I have three babies at home.

85
00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:42.730
They definitely act differently

86
00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:45.130
when I've had scenes with cats

87
00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:48.320 line:15%
when I've been fondling other cats,

88
00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:49.690 line:15%
I'm assuming they're jealous.

89
00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:51.130 line:15%
I think they must smell something.

90
00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.700 line:15%
Is there anything I can do to ease this transition

91
00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:57.761 line:15%
from my cat cafe work to my just cat loving home?

92
00:03:57.761 --> 00:04:00.743
Yeah, my cats do that too.

93
00:04:00.743 --> 00:04:02.440
So I think it's totally normal.

94
00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:04.800
What I do is that,

95
00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.680
I make sure to give them a lot of attention,

96
00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.170
give them treats and play a lot with them

97
00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:11.280
so that they don't stay mad at me.

98
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.750
Christina, how has the business adapted

99
00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:15.440
during the pandemic?

100
00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.440
It's been really a totally challenging year.

101
00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.430
It's been a very different year for us.

102
00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:21.990
Almost exactly a year ago,

103
00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.552
we had to close down our business

104
00:04:24.552 --> 00:04:26.760 line:15%
but when you're in the business of saving lives,

105
00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:29.610 line:15%
sitting at home just does not feel right.

106
00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:30.950 line:15%
So we just went into it

107
00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.820 line:15%
and just started making masks for people.

108
00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.060 line:15%
And we started donating masks, we started selling masks.

109
00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:38.603
We created this entire new enterprise of,

110
00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.770
trying to help people.

111
00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:43.195
In the meantime, we've been answering--

112
00:04:43.195 --> 00:04:44.567 line:15%
Aww, look at him!

113
00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.380 line:15%
We're still doing adoptions

114
00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:51.680 line:15%
and Emily has been doing such an incredible job of

115
00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:54.530 line:15%
going on Zoom, basically seven days a week

116
00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:57.530 line:15%
to help the meet and greet so people could meet their cat.

117
00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.200 line:15%
And we've been doing--
Oh my gosh.

118
00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:01.350 line:15%
I would take that cat right off the screen.

119
00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:02.540 line:15%
I'm not kidding.

120
00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.250 line:15%
That, I don't need any in-person, right there.

121
00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:05.670 line:15%
You'd have to fight me for him.

122
00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:06.973 line:15%
I don't want that cat.

123
00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.360
Well, actually Christina and Emily,

124
00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.985
we and our friends at Cat's Pride,

125
00:05:12.985 --> 00:05:16.360
want to help Meow Parlour continue to do it's great work.

126
00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:20.716
And Cat's Pride would like to donate $10,000

127
00:05:20.716 --> 00:05:24.653
to your organization.
(audience applauding)

128
00:05:24.653 --> 00:05:26.200
Do you hear that, Bandit?

129
00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.120
And that's not all.
Thank you.

130
00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:30.930
They have a Litter for Good program where they,

131
00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:35.100
for every jug of litter sold, they actually donate a pound

132
00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.750
of litter to animal shelters in need.

133
00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.407
And they'd like to give you an additional

134
00:05:39.407 --> 00:05:42.490
$5,000 worth of litter.

135
00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:44.520
Wow, thank you so much.

136
00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:48.310
And when you've got cats, you need litter.

137
00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:50.330
So thank you, Cat's Pride.

138
00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:52.720
And I just want to thank Christina and Emily

139
00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:54.570
for the work that you're doing.

140
00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:57.720
We want to get you back up on those paws.

141
00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.440
And I don't know about anyone else

142
00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:04.890
but I have been clutching my pets on a daily basis.

143
00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:07.530
And we're gonna be thrown a lot of things

144
00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:11.320
through this experience of a ride we're on

145
00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:13.660
but we need those things that make us feel good.

146
00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.960
So thank you, Emily and Christina,

147
00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.320
for all that you're doing.

148
00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:20.767
And Mayim, you make me feel good.

149
00:06:20.767 --> 00:06:21.600
Aw, thank you.

150
00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.710
And I think you're making the world feel less alone

151
00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:27.250
whether it's because they need a laugh on your show

152
00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:28.500
and throughout their lives,

153
00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:30.970
'cause you've been doing that for everyone's life,

154
00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:35.970
or to get real and solve problems on your podcast,

155
00:06:36.737 --> 00:06:39.360
"Mayim Bialik: Breakdown".

156
00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:43.080
It is, whatever your breakdown is,

157
00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:46.447
is lifting everyone else up at the same time.

158
00:06:46.447 --> 00:06:48.810
Thank you so much, such an honor, honor

159
00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:51.820
to speak to you and finally get to connect with you.

160
00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:54.770
I am in awe of you and I was so excited.

161
00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:57.280
The world gave me such a gift today

162
00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:00.600
that I got to talk to you because you saved me as a parent

163
00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.710
and a woman who needed--
Thank you.

164
00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:05.313
I needed salvation in that moment and through it.

165
00:07:05.313 --> 00:07:07.440
I would never kick you in the shins.

166
00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.227
I want you to know that.
(Drew laughing)

167
00:07:10.227 --> 00:07:13.278
"Call Me Kat" Thursdays at 9/8 central on Fox.

168
00:07:13.278 --> 00:07:15.945
(upbeat music)

